Feature: Data Standardization for delivery_dt in f_order Table

  Background:
    Given the f_order table exists in purgo_playground schema of purgo_databricks catalog
    And the f_order table has a column delivery_dt with data type Decimal(38,0)

  Scenario Outline: Validate delivery_dt data type and format
    Given the delivery_dt value is "<delivery_dt>"
    When the SQL logic for data standardization is executed
    Then the delivery_dt should be of type Decimal(38,0)
    And the delivery_dt should match the format "yyyyMMdd"
    And the result should be "<result>"
    And the error message should be "<error_message>"

    Examples:
      | delivery_dt | result    | error_message                               |
      | 20240910    | Pass      |                                             |
      | 2024-09-10  | Fail      | delivery_dt format is not yyyyMMdd          |
      | 2024091     | Fail      | delivery_dt does not match required length  |
      | 202409100   | Fail      | delivery_dt does not match required length  |
      | "20240910"  | Fail      | delivery_dt is not of type Decimal(38,0)     |
      | NULL        | Fail      | delivery_dt value is NULL                   |
      | 20243101    | Pass      |                                             |
      | 20240229    | Pass      |                                             |
      | 20231301    | Fail      | delivery_dt contains invalid month          |
      | 20240000    | Fail      | delivery_dt contains invalid day and month  |

  Scenario: All delivery_dt values are valid
    Given all delivery_dt values in f_order are Decimal(38,0) and in yyyyMMdd format
    When the SQL logic for data standardization is executed
    Then all delivery_dt values should pass the validation
    And no error messages should be generated

  Scenario: Some delivery_dt values have incorrect data type
    Given some delivery_dt values in f_order are not Decimal(38,0)
    When the SQL logic for data standardization is executed
    Then those delivery_dt values should fail the data type validation
    And appropriate error messages should be generated

  Scenario: Some delivery_dt values have incorrect format
    Given some delivery_dt values in f_order are not in yyyyMMdd format
    When the SQL logic for data standardization is executed
    Then those delivery_dt values should fail the format validation
    And appropriate error messages should be generated

  Scenario: delivery_dt contains NULL values
    Given some delivery_dt values in f_order are NULL
    When the SQL logic for data standardization is executed
    Then those delivery_dt values should fail the NULL validation
    And appropriate error messages should be generated

  Scenario: SQL Logic Execution Frequency
    Given the SQL logic is scheduled to run daily
    When the SQL logic for data standardization is executed
    Then the validation should occur without impacting system performance

  Scenario: Execution Trigger on Data Load
    Given new data is loaded into the f_order table
    When the SQL logic for data standardization is triggered
    Then the delivery_dt values in the new data should be validated immediately
    And any failures should be reported promptly

  Scenario: Reporting Validation Results
    Given the SQL logic has been executed
    When validation is complete
    Then the results should be stored in dq_reports table
    And the dq_reports table should reflect the status of delivery_dt validation

  Scenario: Handling Validation Failures
    Given the SQL logic has identified invalid delivery_dt values
    When validation failures are detected
    Then alerts should be sent to the data engineering team
    And the dq_reports table should log the specific error messages

